WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.885
I'm here in Egypt, standing on the Giza Plateau, which is known for its massive pyramids.

2
00:00:06.886 --> 00:00:12.936
The pyramid closest to me is the Pyramid of Khafre, named for the pharaoh who built it.

3
00:00:12.937 --> 00:00:16.716
The farther one is called the Great Pyramid of Giza.

4
00:00:16.717 --> 00:00:20.960
The Pharaoh Khufu—Khafre's father—built that one.

5
00:00:20.961 --> 00:00:27.103
You might find this hard to believe, but these pyramids were built over four thousand years ago.

6
00:00:27.104 --> 00:00:30.303
Hidden in the gray dawn, there's something else.

7
00:00:30.304 --> 00:00:33.503
Do you see it? It's the back of a massive head!

8
00:00:33.504 --> 00:00:37.308
You're looking at the Great Sphinx of Giza!

9
00:00:37.309 --> 00:00:40.868
You've probably already heard of the Great Sphinx of Giza.

10
00:00:40.869 --> 00:00:45.375
It's the tallest stone statue ever built in ancient Egypt.

11
00:00:45.376 --> 00:00:52.600
Scientists believe it was created around 2500 BC, maybe during Pharaoh Khafre's reign.

12
00:00:52.601 --> 00:00:58.193
Carved from limestone, the statue has a lion's body and a person's head.

13
00:00:58.194 --> 00:01:06.845
The Great Sphinx really is "great"; its massive body is about 73 meters long and 20 meters high.

14
00:01:06.846 --> 00:01:14.307
Its head is bigger than a mansion, and its body weighs about the same as fifty jumbo jets!

15
00:01:14.308 --> 00:01:20.615
The sphinx, a mythological creature, first appeared in ancient Egyptian and Greek culture.

16
00:01:20.616 --> 00:01:26.099
In art and stories, the sphinx always has a lion's body and a human's face.

17
00:01:26.100 --> 00:01:35.271
But while the ancient Greeks portrayed the sphinx as female, usually with wings, the ancient Egyptians portrayed the sphinx as male.

18
00:01:35.272 --> 00:01:44.637
Many Egyptian temples and pyramids have sphinx statues standing guard; the ancient Egyptians probably saw them as benevolent protectors.

19
00:01:44.638 --> 00:01:51.415
The appearance of the sphinx in culture has given scientists clues about the Great Sphinx monument.

20
00:01:51.416 --> 00:01:59.096
But many mysteries still surround it. For instance, scholars wonder about the Sphinx's face.

21
00:01:59.097 --> 00:02:01.460
Was it carved to look like a real person?

22
00:02:01.461 --> 00:02:05.625
Perhaps Pharaoh Khafre or his father, Pharaoh Khufu?

23
00:02:05.626 --> 00:02:10.083
Many experts suspect the Sphinx has Khafre's face.

24
00:02:10.084 --> 00:02:14.925
That's because Khafre had a beard, and so did the statue, originally.

25
00:02:14.926 --> 00:02:23.125
Why was the statue built? Maybe it was constructed to honor the pharaoh—a symbol of his awesome power.

26
00:02:23.126 --> 00:02:27.360
Or perhaps it was put there, facing east, to worship the sun.

27
00:02:27.361 --> 00:02:33.790
In ancient Egypt, the horizon was believed to be where the dead entered the afterlife.

28
00:02:33.791 --> 00:02:37.632
The Great Sphinx could be guarding that sacred spot.

29
00:02:37.633 --> 00:02:48.818
And who built the Great Sphinx? While the nearby pyramids have inscriptions and clues about their builders, the Great Sphinx reveals almost no clues.

30
00:02:48.819 --> 00:02:54.332
Scientists think it was created by the same team that constructed one of the pyramids.

31
00:02:54.333 --> 00:03:01.183
But since these pyramids were built at different times, it's hard to know for sure which team that was.

32
00:03:01.184 --> 00:03:07.338
And here's another mystery about the Sphinx's construction—it was never finished.

33
00:03:07.339 --> 00:03:13.829
Scholars don't know why, but the builders seem to have abandoned the project shortly before its completion.

34
00:03:13.830 --> 00:03:21.663
I was surprised to learn this, but sand has buried the Great Sphinx on and off throughout most of its existence.

35
00:03:21.664 --> 00:03:31.267
According to a story from around 1400 BC, a prince was hunting in the hot desert and saw the Sphinx's head sticking out of the sand.

36
00:03:31.268 --> 00:03:34.565
He decided to sit in the shade under the head.

37
00:03:34.566 --> 00:03:42.698
The prince fell asleep, and when the sun reached its highest point, the statue appeared to the prince in a dream.

38
00:03:42.699 --> 00:03:49.799
It said that if the prince uncovered the rest of the statue, the prince would become the next pharaoh.

39
00:03:49.800 --> 00:03:56.388
The prince did as the statue said, and he became King Thutmose IV!

40
00:03:56.389 --> 00:04:02.037
Oh, and over time the Great Sphinx was buried under sand again, of course!

41
00:04:02.042 --> 00:04:06.378
Being buried under the sand may have helped to protect the Sphinx.

42
00:04:06.379 --> 00:04:12.570
If the Sphinx had not been buried for most of its existence, it would have disappeared long ago.

43
00:04:12.577 --> 00:04:17.333
Still, the statue has suffered a lot of damage over time.

44
00:04:17.334 --> 00:04:22.920
Its nose is missing—gone forever, probably chiseled out by looters.

45
00:04:22.921 --> 00:04:29.002
But that's not the worst problem. The statue is slowly turning to dust!

46
00:04:29.003 --> 00:04:35.017
Limestone is soft, and wind, water, and sand have weakened the statue over time.

47
00:04:35.018 --> 00:04:40.574
Two more recent threats to the Great Sphinx are pollution and rising groundwater.

48
00:04:40.575 --> 00:04:46.344
Today the stone is treated with special chemicals that help protect it from the pollution.

49
00:04:46.345 --> 00:04:52.261
And holes have been drilled in several spots near the statue to prevent water damage.

50
00:04:52.262 --> 00:05:00.229
Luckily, scientists also used sophisticated laser scanning equipment to closely examine the statue.

51
00:05:00.230 --> 00:05:08.100
The equipment helped to identify its weak spots, and now scientists can take steps to limit future damage.

52
00:05:08.101 --> 00:05:18.052
Thousands of years ago, as the Great Sphinx sat here, gazing at the rising sun, it was probably guarding the pharaohs' entryway to the afterlife.

53
00:05:18.053 --> 00:05:20.892
Now it's our time to be the guards.

54
00:05:20.893 --> 00:05:25.863
We have to watch the ancient Sphinx carefully and take good care of it.

55
00:05:25.864 --> 00:05:35.340
That way, thousands of years from now, people will still be admiring its beauty.

